sweet-pcsamp-procs (lowclk 2026-11-14, tracker L-08 follow-up): boot-arg sweetpcsampproc=a,b,c makes the 0263 CPU PC sampler (sweetpcsamp=N) watch up to 3 other processes
instead of backboardd / SpringBoard / Preferences. Why [observed, f1aa]: the process snapshot sampler 0054 cannot see a running thread (no saved user state), 23 of 27 coreduetd samples read pc 0x0;
the PC sampler reads the interrupted state in the IPI, so it can see coreduetd's busy thread, MobileTimer and Preferences during the 1-3 s waits after an app open. R0: read-only sampler, no
register access, no hardware write; the only new input is a boot-arg string (PE_parse_boot_arg_str, force-string, max_len copy, read from pexpert/gen/bootargs.c xnu-8796).
Syntax: comma list, up to 3 names, compared like 0263 (strncmp(p_comm, name, MAXCOMLEN), so a name is at most MAXCOMLEN = 16 characters). Absent: today's three processes, rows and header
byte for byte as before (keys bb sb pf). Set: slot keys are p0 p1 p2 in every row and in the header (`t N rounds R reached C hits H p0 A p1 B p2 C entries E dropped D`) and one line at start,
`SWEET PCSAMP: slots p0=<name> p1=<name> p2=<name>` (an unused slot prints `-` and matches nothing; the period line then says `processes as in the slots line (boot-arg sweetpcsampproc)`).
GAPs (rule 7): `SWEET GAP: sweetpcsampproc '<arg>': ...` for an empty entry (skipped), a name longer than MAXCOMLEN (skipped), more than 3 entries (the first 3 valid names are used), no valid name
(the three defaults are used, keys still p0 p1 p2) and an argument cut at 127 characters. Host: tools/test_pcsamp_procs_core.py compiles the SWEET_PCSAMP_PARSE block of this patch; tools/pcsamp-sym
reads both header forms and maps p0/p1/p2 through the slots line. Not run on hardware (tag: guess until a boot shows the rows).
